  "question": {
    "text": "The mean and variance of seven&nbsp;observations are <math><mn>8</mn></math> and <math><mn>16</mn></math> respectively. If five&nbsp;of the observations are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>12</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn></math>, then the remaining two&nbsp;observations are"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>7</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>8</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math><mi>x</mi></math> and <math><mi>y</mi></math> be remaining <math><mn>2</mn></math> observations<br />Mean <math><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo></math> <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></math>&nbsp;...(i)<br />Variance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>8</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo></math> <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></math>&nbsp;...(ii)<br />now solving equation (i) and (ii),&nbsp;we get,</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p>"
  }
}